cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite this repository.
type: software
title: 'What Makes Edge Coordination Resilient? Software and synthetic data'
repository-code: https://github.com/fnuni/2026diot
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Nucci
    given-names: Francesco
    email: francesco.nucci@unisalento.it
    affiliation: 'Department of Engineering for Innovation, University of Salento'
  - family-names: Papadia
    given-names: Gabriele
    email: gabriele.papadia@unisalento.it
    affiliation: 'Department of Engineering for Innovation, University of Salento'
abstract: >-
  Deterministic multi-agent simulator of home healthcare dispatch with vehicle
  agents, a fog coordinator and a cloud optimiser, an ownership-token protocol
  for at-most-once service under partitions and a two-node vaccine-carrier model
  with a conditional linear thermal bound. Includes a two-phase synthetic study
  (10,192 screening runs and 2,660 completed-service C1-C3 runs),
  an outage-only greedy fallback, primary and exploratory analyses, run tables,
  analyses, raw replay logs for reported seed 9001 and tests.
  Synthetic data are licensed CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - classical deliberative agents
  - edge computing
  - fog computing
  - multi-agent systems
  - home healthcare routing
  - vaccine cold chain
  - reproducible simulation
